    },
    {
      "unit_id": "SU-P014-GEAR-003",
      "unit_type": "paragraph",
      "unit_scope": "in_scope_text",
      "reading_order": 3,
      "source_block_id": "P014-B001",
      "source_region_ids": [
        "PRM-G1-VIRAL-001-P014-R01"
      ],
      "crop_ids": [
        "P014-B001-TES"
      ],
      "text": "These bits of equipment are carried by the Krew based on their job (see Investigator descriptions).",
      "heading_level": null,
      "display_style": "body",
      "text_source_state": "machine_reviewed_delegated"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "SU-P014-GEAR-004",
      "unit_type": "heading",
      "unit_scope": "in_scope_text",
      "reading_order": 4,
      "source_block_id": "P014-B002",
      "source_region_ids": [
        "PRM-G1-VIRAL-001-P014-R02"
      ],
      "crop_ids": [
        "P014-B002-TES"
      ],
      "text": "Equipment Satchel",
      "heading_level": "h4",
      "display_style": "section_heading",
      "text_source_state": "machine_reviewed_delegated",
      "layout_role": "block_heading",
      "font_style": "normal",
      "line_break_after": true
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "SU-P014-GEAR-005",
      "unit_type": "paragraph",
      "unit_scope": "in_scope_text",
      "reading_order": 5,
      "source_block_id": "P014-B002",
      "source_region_ids": [
        "PRM-G1-VIRAL-001-P014-R02"
      ],
      "crop_ids": [
        "P014-B002-TES"
      ],
      "text": "Each team member has a black canvas satchel (with the Spektral Krew logo of course) for carrying their gear. In some cases, the host may hand off his satchel to someone else while they're on camera. It's big enough to hold the Handheld Night Vision Cameras, EMF Meters, Smart Phones, and FLIR Cameras, plus any other personal gear.",
      "heading_level": null,
      "display_style": "body",
      "text_source_state": "machine_reviewed_delegated"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "SU-P014-GEAR-006",
      "unit_type": "heading",
      "unit_scope": "in_scope_text",
      "reading_order": 6,
      "source_block_id": "P014-B003",
      "source_region_ids": [
        "PRM-G1-VIRAL-001-P014-R03"
      ],
      "crop_ids": [
        "P014-B003-TES"
      ],
      "text": "Handheld Night Vision Cameras (2)",
      "heading_level": "h4",
      "display_style": "section_heading",
      "text_source_state": "machine_reviewed_delegated",
      "layout_role": "block_heading",
      "font_style": "normal",
      "line_break_after": true
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "SU-P014-GEAR-007",
      "unit_type": "paragraph",
      "unit_scope": "in_scope_text",
      "reading_order": 7,
      "source_block_id": "P014-B003",
      "source_region_ids": [
        "PRM-G1-VIRAL-001-P014-R03"
      ],
      "crop_ids": [
        "P014-B003-TES"
      ],
      "text": "4K Wi-Fi Full Spectrum Camcorders, Ultra HD Infrared Night Vision Paranormal Investigation Video Camera with 60 fps 24 MP 30x Digital Zoom. Peter and Enoch usually carry and operate these. [Four Hours of Battery Life]",
      "heading_level": null,
      "display_style": "body",
      "text_source_state": "machine_reviewed_delegated"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "SU-P014-GEAR-008",
      "unit_type": "heading",
      "unit_scope": "in_scope_text",
      "reading_order": 8,
      "source_block_id": "P014-B003",
      "source_region_ids": [
        "PRM-G1-VIRAL-001-P014-R03"
      ],
      "crop_ids": [
        "P014-B003-TES"
      ],
      "text": "EMF Meter",
      "heading_level": "h4",
      "display_style": "section_heading",
      "text_source_state": "machine_reviewed_delegated",
      "layout_role": "block_heading",
      "font_style": "normal",
      "line_break_after": true
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "SU-P014-GEAR-009",
      "unit_type": "paragraph",
      "unit_scope": "in_scope_text",
      "reading_order": 9,
      "source_block_id": "P014-B003",
      "source_region_ids": [
        "PRM-G1-VIRAL-001-P014-R03"
      ],
      "crop_ids": [
        "P014-B003-TES"
      ],
      "text": "HF-B3G Triple Axis HF RF Power Meter Analyzer and Detector. [12 Hours of Battery Life]",
      "heading_level": null,
      "display_style": "body",
      "text_source_state": "machine_reviewed_delegated"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "SU-P014-GEAR-010",
      "unit_type": "heading",
      "unit_scope": "in_scope_text",
      "reading_order": 10,
      "source_block_id": "P014-B004",
      "source_region_ids": [
        "PRM-G1-VIRAL-001-P014-R04"
      ],
      "crop_ids": [
        "P014-B004-TES"
      ],
      "text": "Keeper's Notes",
      "heading_level": "h4",
      "display_style": "callout_heading",
      "text_source_state": "machine_reviewed_delegated",
      "layout_role": "block_heading",
      "font_style": "bold",
      "line_break_after": true
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "SU-P014-GEAR-011",
      "unit_type": "paragraph",
      "unit_scope": "in_scope_text",
      "reading_order": 11,
      "source_block_id": "P014-B004",
      "source_region_ids": [
        "PRM-G1-VIRAL-001-P014-R04"
      ],
      "crop_ids": [
        "P014-B004-TES"
      ],
      "text": "There are not many EMFs on the island, but the Krew will see the odd tick here and there from background noise. While ghosts don't generate electromagnetic fields, Hastalyk can use this against the Investigators by causing it to respond in the direction it wants them to go. Marco is usually in possession of this.",
      "heading_level": null,
      "display_style": "callout_body",
      "text_source_state": "machine_reviewed_delegated",
      "semantic_split_contract": {
        "contract": "semantic_segmentation_contract.v1",
        "segment_type": "bounded_callout_body",
        "callout_heading": "Keeper's Notes",
        "boundary_kind": "callout_extends_to_text_block_end",
        "boundary_marker": "<text_block_end>"
      }
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "SU-P014-GEAR-012",
      "unit_type": "heading",
      "unit_scope": "in_scope_text",
      "reading_order": 12,
      "source_block_id": "P014-B005",
      "source_region_ids": [
        "PRM-G1-VIRAL-001-P014-R05"
      ],
      "crop_ids": [
        "P014-B005-TES"
      ],
      "text": "Spirit Box",
      "heading_level": "h4",
      "display_style": "section_heading",
      "text_source_state": "machine_reviewed_delegated",
      "layout_role": "block_heading",
      "font_style": "normal",
      "line_break_after": true
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "SU-P014-GEAR-013",
      "unit_type": "paragraph",
      "unit_scope": "in_scope_text",
      "reading_order": 13,
      "source_block_id": "P014-B005",
      "source_region_ids": [
        "PRM-G1-VIRAL-001-P014-R05"
      ],
      "crop_ids": [
        "P014-B005-TES"
      ],
      "text": "This is a custom radio with a frequency scan mode that the Krew hopes will allow them to communicate with spirits. It's about the size of a walkie-talkie and includes a headphone to better hear voices from the beyond. [Eight Hours of Battery Life]",
      "heading_level": null,
      "display_style": "body",
      "text_source_state": "machine_reviewed_delegated"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "SU-P014-GEAR-014",
      "unit_type": "heading",
      "unit_scope": "in_scope_text",
      "reading_order": 14,
      "source_block_id": "P014-B005",
      "source_region_ids": [
        "PRM-G1-VIRAL-001-P014-R05"
      ],
      "crop_ids": [
        "P014-B005-TES"
      ],
      "text": "Keeper's Notes",
      "heading_level": "h4",
      "display_style": "callout_heading",
      "text_source_state": "machine_reviewed_delegated",
      "layout_role": "block_heading",
      "font_style": "bold",
      "line_break_after": true
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "SU-P014-GEAR-015",
      "unit_type": "paragraph",
      "unit_scope": "in_scope_text",
      "reading_order": 15,
      "source_block_id": "P014-B005",
      "source_region_ids": [
        "PRM-G1-VIRAL-001-P014-R05"
      ],
      "crop_ids": [
        "P014-B005-TES"
      ],
      "text": "It's possible that the Spirit Box could pick up radio chatter from the Italian military or the Plague Monk chanting various disturbing litanies in Latin (Keeper's discretion).",
      "heading_level": null,
      "display_style": "callout_body",
      "text_source_state": "machine_reviewed_delegated",
      "semantic_split_contract": {
        "contract": "semantic_segmentation_contract.v1",
        "segment_type": "bounded_callout_body",
        "callout_heading": "Keeper's Notes",
        "boundary_kind": "callout_extends_to_text_block_end",
        "boundary_marker": "<text_block_end>"
      }
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "SU-P014-GEAR-016",
      "unit_type": "heading",
      "unit_scope": "in_scope_text",
      "reading_order": 16,
      "source_block_id": "P014-B006",
      "source_region_ids": [
        "PRM-G1-VIRAL-001-P014-R06"
      ],
      "crop_ids": [
        "P014-B006-TES"
      ],
      "text": "EVP Recorder SCD1",
      "heading_level": "h4",
      "display_style": "section_heading",
      "text_source_state": "machine_reviewed_delegated",
      "layout_role": "block_heading",
      "font_style": "normal",
      "line_break_after": true
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "SU-P014-GEAR-017",
      "unit_type": "paragraph",
      "unit_scope": "in_scope_text",
      "reading_order": 17,
      "source_block_id": "P014-B006",
      "source_region_ids": [
        "PRM-G1-VIRAL-001-P014-R06"
      ],
      "crop_ids": [
        "P014-B006-TES"
      ],
      "text": "The SCD1 is an experimental piece of equipment that Marco has had someone build - it is the Silent Capture Device. The processor and software can detect when nobody is talking and will flash when it picks up a sound during silence. This can be played back in real time. This was an expensive piece of prototype technology, so Marco keeps hold of this.",
      "heading_level": null,
      "display_style": "body",
      "text_source_state": "machine_reviewed_delegated"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "SU-P014-GEAR-018",
      "unit_type": "heading",
      "unit_scope": "in_scope_text",
      "reading_order": 18,
      "source_block_id": "P014-B006",
      "source_region_ids": [
        "PRM-G1-VIRAL-001-P014-R06"
      ],
      "crop_ids": [
        "P014-B006-TES"
      ],
      "text": "FLIR Camera for Smartphone",
      "heading_level": "h4",
      "display_style": "section_heading",
      "text_source_state": "machine_reviewed_delegated",
      "layout_role": "block_heading",
      "font_style": "normal",
      "line_break_after": true
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "SU-P014-GEAR-019",
      "unit_type": "paragraph",
      "unit_scope": "in_scope_text",
      "reading_order": 19,
      "source_block_id": "P014-B006",
      "source_region_ids": [
        "PRM-G1-VIRAL-001-P014-R06"
      ],
      "crop_ids": [
        "P014-B006-TES"
      ],
      "text": "FLIR ONE Pro - iOS - Professional Grade Thermal Camera for Smartphones - with VividIR and MSX Image Enhancement Technology. This has been jury rigged by Hyeon so that it uses the video feed from Peter's camera. [Battery Life of the FLIR is only 45 Minutes]",
      "heading_level": null,
      "display_style": "body",
      "text_source_state": "machine_reviewed_delegated"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "SU-P014-GEAR-020",
      "unit_type": "heading",
      "unit_scope": "in_scope_text",
      "reading_order": 20,
      "source_block_id": "P014-B007",
      "source_region_ids": [
        "PRM-G1-VIRAL-001-P014-R07"
      ],
      "crop_ids": [
        "P014-B007-TES"
      ],
      "text": "Static",
      "heading_level": "h3",
      "display_style": "section_heading",
      "text_source_state": "machine_reviewed_delegated",
      "layout_role": "block_heading",
      "font_style": "normal",
      "line_break_after": true
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "SU-P014-GEAR-021",
      "unit_type": "paragraph",
      "unit_scope": "in_scope_text",
      "reading_order": 21,
      "source_block_id": "P014-B007",
      "source_region_ids": [
        "PRM-G1-VIRAL-001-P014-R07"
      ],
      "crop_ids": [
        "P014-B007-TES"
      ],
      "text": "These bits of equipment are set up early on and, with the exception of the drone, remain at a single location.",
      "heading_level": null,
      "display_style": "body",
      "text_source_state": "machine_reviewed_delegated"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "SU-P014-GEAR-022",
      "unit_type": "heading",
      "unit_scope": "in_scope_text",
      "reading_order": 22,
      "source_block_id": "P014-B007",
      "source_region_ids": [
        "PRM-G1-VIRAL-001-P014-R07"
      ],
      "crop_ids": [
        "P014-B007-TES"
      ],
      "text": "Base Station",
      "heading_level": "h4",
      "display_style": "section_heading",
      "text_source_state": "machine_reviewed_delegated",
      "layout_role": "block_heading",
      "font_style": "normal",
      "line_break_after": true
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "SU-P014-GEAR-023",
      "unit_type": "paragraph",
      "unit_scope": "in_scope_text",
      "reading_order": 23,
      "source_block_id": "P014-B007",
      "source_region_ids": [
        "PRM-G1-VIRAL-001-P014-R07"
      ],
      "crop_ids": [
        "P014-B007-TES"
      ],
      "text": "This is a custom industrial laptop with a Wi-Fi hub and satellite uplink set up for live streaming. A deep cycle battery unit supplies enough power for up to 12 hours of continuous broadcasting.",
      "heading_level": null,
      "display_style": "body",
      "text_source_state": "machine_reviewed_delegated"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "SU-P014-GEAR-024",
      "unit_type": "heading",
      "unit_scope": "in_scope_text",
      "reading_order": 24,
      "source_block_id": "P014-B007",
      "source_region_ids": [
        "PRM-G1-VIRAL-001-P014-R07"
      ],
      "crop_ids": [
        "P014-B007-TES"
      ],
      "text": "Keeper's Notes",
      "heading_level": "h4",
      "display_style": "callout_heading",
      "text_source_state": "machine_reviewed_delegated",
      "layout_role": "block_heading",
      "font_style": "bold",
      "line_break_after": true
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "SU-P014-GEAR-025",
      "unit_type": "paragraph",
      "unit_scope": "in_scope_text",
      "reading_order": 25,
      "source_block_id": "P014-B007",
      "source_region_ids": [
        "PRM-G1-VIRAL-001-P014-R07"
      ],
      "crop_ids": [
        "P014-B007-TES"
      ],
      "text": "At the Keeper's discretion, other devices may be charged off the base station's battery, but this obviously takes time that the Investigators may not have.",
      "heading_level": null,
      "display_style": "callout_body",
      "text_source_state": "machine_reviewed_delegated",
      "semantic_split_contract": {
        "contract": "semantic_segmentation_contract.v1",
        "segment_type": "bounded_callout_body",
        "callout_heading": "Keeper's Notes",
        "boundary_kind": "callout_extends_to_text_block_end",
        "boundary_marker": "<text_block_end>"
      }
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "SU-P014-GEAR-026",
      "unit_type": "heading",
      "unit_scope": "in_scope_text",
      "reading_order": 26,
      "source_block_id": "P014-B008",
      "source_region_ids": [
        "PRM-G1-VIRAL-001-P014-R08"
      ],
      "crop_ids": [
        "P014-B008-TES"
      ],
      "text": "Cellular Wi-Fi Repeaters/Transmitters (2)",
      "heading_level": "h4",
      "display_style": "section_heading",
      "text_source_state": "machine_reviewed_delegated",
      "layout_role": "block_heading",
      "font_style": "normal",
      "line_break_after": true
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "SU-P014-GEAR-027",
      "unit_type": "paragraph",
      "unit_scope": "in_scope_text",
      "reading_order": 27,
      "source_block_id": "P014-B008",
      "source_region_ids": [
        "PRM-G1-VIRAL-001-P014-R08"
      ],
      "crop_ids": [
        "P014-B008-TES"
      ],
      "text": "Each provides Wi-Fi within a 300 Meter radius, and has a battery unit that provides 8-10 hours of uninterrupted signal.",
      "heading_level": null,
      "display_style": "body",
      "text_source_state": "machine_reviewed_delegated"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "SU-P014-GEAR-028",
      "unit_type": "heading",
      "unit_scope": "in_scope_text",
      "reading_order": 28,
      "source_block_id": "P014-B008",
      "source_region_ids": [
        "PRM-G1-VIRAL-001-P014-R08"
      ],
      "crop_ids": [
        "P014-B008-TES"
      ],
      "text": "Keeper's Notes",
      "heading_level": "h4",
      "display_style": "callout_heading",
      "text_source_state": "machine_reviewed_delegated",
      "layout_role": "block_heading",
      "font_style": "bold",
      "line_break_after": true
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "SU-P014-GEAR-029",
      "unit_type": "paragraph",
      "unit_scope": "in_scope_text",
      "reading_order": 29,
      "source_block_id": "P014-B008",
      "source_region_ids": [
        "PRM-G1-VIRAL-001-P014-R08"
      ],
      "crop_ids": [
        "P014-B008-TES"
      ],
      "text": "These are best set up in three key locations, the lighthouse, the far side of the bridge, and the hospital tower. This provides the greatest area of coverage for the investigation site. Note that since the satellite signal is being routed through the Base Station at the lighthouse, the hospital signal requires the bridge transmitter to be active.",
      "heading_level": null,
      "display_style": "callout_body",
      "text_source_state": "machine_reviewed_delegated",
      "semantic_split_contract": {
        "contract": "semantic_segmentation_contract.v1",
        "segment_type": "bounded_callout_body",
        "callout_heading": "Keeper's Notes",
        "boundary_kind": "callout_extends_to_text_block_end",
        "boundary_marker": "<text_block_end>"
      }
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "SU-P014-GEAR-030",
      "unit_type": "heading",
      "unit_scope": "in_scope_text",
      "reading_order": 30,
      "source_block_id": "P014-B009",
      "source_region_ids": [
        "PRM-G1-VIRAL-001-P014-R09"
      ],
      "crop_ids": [
        "P014-B009-TES"
      ],
      "text": "UPS Batteries (3)",
      "heading_level": "h4",
      "display_style": "section_heading",
      "text_source_state": "machine_reviewed_delegated",
      "layout_role": "block_heading",
      "font_style": "normal",
      "line_break_after": true
    },
    {
      "unit_id": "SU-P014-GEAR-031",
      "unit_type": "paragraph",
      "unit_scope": "in_scope_text",
      "reading_order": 31,
      "source_block_id": "P014-B009",
      "source_region_ids": [
        "PRM-G1-VIRAL-001-P014-R09"
      ],
      "crop_ids": [
        "P014-B009-TES"
      ],
      "text": "Primarily used to power the Wi-Fi Transmitters, they have various connections via which other equipment can be recharged. They can provide around six hours of power each in the event of power failure. Really only there in the instance of the battery backup for the hub failing. Extremely heavy as they are essentially large deep-cycle batteries.",
